Q: How to use java .class file in Visual Studio Code? A: <p>Assume you have a class file <code>x/y/A.class</code>, so a class <code>A</code> with package <code>x.y</code> with a class <code>B</code> inside.</p>
<pre><code>import x.y.A; // When only using A.
import x.y.A.B; //  When using B.
</code></pre>
<p>One could also use s static import, actually importing <strong>all</strong> declarations inside <code>A</code>.</p>
<pre><code>import static x.y.A.*;
</code></pre>
<h3>What different kinds of inner classes with respect to the outer A.</h3>
<p>If you do not know that <code>B</code> is there, this might help finding <code>B</code> in the IDE using <kbd>Ctrl</kbd><kbd>Space</kbd>.</p>
<p>The source of A could have been one of:</p>
<ul>
<li><p>A non-public class on the same level: <em>not our case!</em></p>
<pre><code>public class A { }
class B { }
</code></pre>
</li>
<li><p>An inner class: <em>accesses the A object via <code>A.this</code></em>.</p>
<pre><code>public class A {
    public class B {
        ... A.this ...
        ... an ...
    }
    int an;
}
A a = new A();
a.new B();
</code></pre>
</li>
<li><p>An static inner class: _accesses the A object via <code>A.this</code>.</p>
<pre><code>public class A {
    public static class B {
        ...
    }
}
new B();
</code></pre>
</li>
</ul>
<p>It could be that there is no default constructor (without arguments), but then again the IDE might help.</p>
<h3>Java's own coded introspection <em>&quot;reflection&quot;</em></h3>
<p>Of course <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Reflective_programming" rel="nofollow noreferrer">reflective programming</a> via <a href="https://docs.oracle.com/javase/tutorial/reflect/" rel="nofollow noreferrer"><em>Java Reflection API</em></a> can be used to inspect the class <code>A</code>; find <code>B</code> and so on.</p>

Q: How to Implement a Typing Animation in Flutter Bloc Without State Skips? A: <p>The issue isn't that Bloc is &quot;optimizing&quot; your states away, but rather how Dart handles object equality and how Bloc uses it to decide whether to notify listeners.</p>
<p>If you mutate a <code>StringBuffer</code> or a <code>List</code> in-place, the reference to that object remains the same. If your <code>ChatState</code> uses equality checks (like <code>Equatable</code> or a custom <code>==</code>), it will see the same object reference and assume nothing changed.</p>
<p>To fix this, you must treat your state as immutable. Instead of appending to the existing <code>StringBuffer</code>, create a new list and a new message object for every piece of the stream:</p>
<pre class="lang-dart prettyprint-override"><code>on&lt;UpdateAiMessageEvent&gt;((event, emit) {
  final updatedMessages = List&lt;Message&gt;.from(state.messages);

  if (updatedMessages.isNotEmpty &amp;&amp; updatedMessages.last.isAi) {
    final lastMessage = updatedMessages.removeLast();
    // Create a NEW message instance with the appended text
    updatedMessages.add(lastMessage.copyWith(
      content: lastMessage.content + event.pieceOfMessage,
    ));
  } else {
    updatedMessages.add(Message(role: Role.assistant, content: event.pieceOfMessage));
  }

  // Emitting a NEW list instance ensures the Bloc notifies the UI
  emit(AiMessageUpdated(messages: updatedMessages));
});
</code></pre>
<p>By ensuring the <code>List</code> and the <code>Message</code> are new instances, <code>BlocBuilder</code> will always receive the update, and Flutter will render the &quot;typing&quot; animation as fast as its frame rate allows.</p>
<h1>Bridging the Network Stream (Retrofit/Dio)</h1>
<p>To make this work with a real backend (like OpenAI's streaming API), you need to transform the raw byte stream from your network client into a stream of strings that your Bloc can consume.</p>
<p><strong>The Retrofit Correction (Critical)</strong></p>
<p>In my original question, I used <code>Stream&lt;String&gt;</code>. This is a common mistake. For true real-time streaming (like OpenAI's Server-Sent Events), you must use <code>Future&lt;HttpResponse&lt;Object&gt;&gt;</code> combined with the <code>@DioResponseType(ResponseType.stream)</code> annotation.</p>
<p><em>Correct Retrofit Client:</em></p>
<pre class="lang-dart prettyprint-override"><code>@RestApi()
abstract class RetrofitClient {
  factory RetrofitClient(Dio dio, {String baseUrl}) = _RetrofitClient;

  @POST('chat')
  @DioResponseType(ResponseType.stream) // This is mandatory for real-time chunks
  Future&lt;HttpResponse&lt;Object&gt;&gt; sendChatMessage(@Body() ChatRequest chatRequest);
}
</code></pre>
<p><em>Transforming the Network Stream</em></p>
<p>In your Repository, you convert the raw ResponseBody into a Stream&lt;String&gt; that the Bloc can consume:</p>
<pre><code>// repository_impl.dart
Stream&lt;String&gt; processResponse(Future&lt;HttpResponse&lt;Object&gt;&gt; responseFuture) async* {
  final HttpResponse&lt;Object&gt; response = await responseFuture;
  final Object data = response.data;

  if (data is ResponseBody) {
    yield* data.stream
        .cast&lt;List&lt;int&gt;&gt;()
        .transform(const Utf8Decoder())
        .transform(const LineSplitter())
        .map((String line) {
          // Logic to extract content from your specific API format
          // Example: 0:&quot;hello&quot; -&gt; hello
          final RegExp regex = RegExp(r'^\d+:&quot;(.+)&quot;$');
          final RegExpMatch? match = regex.firstMatch(line);
          return match?.group(1) ?? '';
        });
  }
}
</code></pre>
<p>This repository returns a <code>Stream&lt;String&gt;</code>. In your Bloc's <code>on&lt;SendMessageEvent&gt;</code>, you simply listen to this stream and add an <code>UpdateAiMessageEvent</code> for every chunk:</p>
<pre class="lang-dart prettyprint-override"><code>_chatRepository.sendChat(chat).listen(
  (chunk) =&gt; add(UpdateAiMessageEvent(chunk)),
  onError: (error) =&gt; add(ErrorEvent(error.toString())),
);
</code></pre>
<p>By combining this Stream Transformation in the Repository with Immutable State Updates in the Bloc, you get a clean, reactive architecture that handles real-time UI updates without ever leaving the Bloc pattern.</p>
<p><strong>Summary:</strong></p>
<p>• Retrofit: Use Future&lt;HttpResponse&lt;Object&gt;&gt; + ResponseType.stream.</p>
<p>• Repository: Decode the ResponseBody stream manually.</p>
<p>• Bloc: Use strict immutability. No !, no in-place mutations.</p>
<p>By doing this, the &quot;Flutter pipeline&quot; will have no trouble rendering every single state change as a smooth typing animation.</p>
<h1><strong>Minimal Reproducible Example</strong></h1>
<p>This example uses only <code>flutter_bloc</code>. You can copy this into a single <code>main.dart</code> to see it in action.</p>
<pre class="lang-dart prettyprint-override"><code>import 'dart:async';
import 'package:flutter/material.dart';
import 'package:flutter_bloc/flutter_bloc.dart';

// --- Entities ---
@immutable
class Message {
  final String content;
  final bool isAi;

  const Message({required this.content, this.isAi = false});

  Message copyWith({String? content}) {
    return Message(
      content: content ?? this.content,
      isAi: isAi,
    );
  }
}

// --- Bloc ---
@immutable
class ChatState {
  final List&lt;Message&gt; messages;
  const ChatState(this.messages);
}

abstract class ChatEvent {}
class SendMessage extends ChatEvent {}
class _UpdateChunk extends ChatEvent {
  final String chunk;
  _UpdateChunk(this.chunk);
}

class ChatBloc extends Bloc&lt;ChatEvent, ChatState&gt; {
  ChatBloc() : super(const ChatState(&lt;Message&gt;[])) {
    on&lt;SendMessage&gt;((SendMessage event, Emitter&lt;ChatState&gt; emit) {
      final List&lt;Message&gt; updated = List&lt;Message&gt;.from(state.messages)
        ..add(const Message(content: &quot;User: Start typing!&quot;, isAi: false));
      emit(ChatState(updated));

      // Simulate stream from a Repository
      _simulateAiStream().listen((String chunk) =&gt; add(_UpdateChunk(chunk)));
    });

    on&lt;_UpdateChunk&gt;((_UpdateChunk event, Emitter&lt;ChatState&gt; emit) {
      final List&lt;Message&gt; messages = List&lt;Message&gt;.from(state.messages);

      if (messages.isNotEmpty &amp;&amp; (messages.lastOrNull?.isAi ?? false)) {
        final Message lastMessage = messages.removeLast();
        // CRITICAL: Create a NEW Message instance to trigger equality change
        messages.add(lastMessage.copyWith(
          content: lastMessage.content + event.chunk,
        ));
      } else {
        messages.add(Message(content: event.chunk, isAi: true));
      }
      emit(ChatState(messages));
    });
  }

  Stream&lt;String&gt; _simulateAiStream() async* {
    final List&lt;String&gt; characters = &quot;This is a typing animation in Bloc!&quot;.split('');
    for (final String char in characters) {
      await Future&lt;void&gt;.delayed(const Duration(milliseconds: 50));
      yield char;
    }
  }
}

// --- UI ---
void main() =&gt; runApp(const MaterialApp(home: BlocTypingPage()));

class BlocTypingPage extends StatelessWidget {
  const BlocTypingPage({super.key});

  @override
  Widget build(BuildContext context) {
    return BlocProvider&lt;ChatBloc&gt;(
      create: (_) =&gt; ChatBloc(),
      child: Scaffold(
        appBar: AppBar(title: const Text(&quot;Bloc Typing Animation&quot;)),
        body: const ChatView(),
      ),
    );
  }
}

class ChatView extends StatelessWidget {
  const ChatView({super.key});

  @override
  Widget build(BuildContext context) {
    return Column(
      children: &lt;Widget&gt;[
        Expanded(
          child: BlocBuilder&lt;ChatBloc, ChatState&gt;(
            builder: (BuildContext context, ChatState state) {
              return ListView.builder(
                itemCount: state.messages.length,
                itemBuilder: (BuildContext _, int index) {
                  final Message message = state.messages[index];
                  return ListTile(
                    title: Text(message.isAi ? &quot;AI&quot; : &quot;You&quot;),
                    subtitle: Text(message.content),
                  );
                },
              );
            },
          ),
        ),
        Padding(
          padding: const EdgeInsets.all(16.0),
          child: ElevatedButton(
            onPressed: () =&gt; context.read&lt;ChatBloc&gt;().add(SendMessage()),
            child: const Text(&quot;Start Typing Effect&quot;),
          ),
        ),
      ],
    );
  }
}
</code></pre>
